cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the accompanying paper."
title: "Active-Learning Surrogate Competition for Cell-Media Titer Optimisation"
abstract: >-
  Code accompanying the Bioinformatics submission "Benchmarking active-learning
  surrogates for cell-media titer optimisation". Implements two competition
  protocols (Hide-the-Label and Open-Race) under two difficulty regimes
  (Regular Mode and Hard Mode) across six published cell-culture / cell-media
  datasets, with surrogate families spanning Gaussian processes, random
  forests, neural networks, and Bayesian neural networks, and a wide pool of
  acquisition strategies (BO, DOE, evolutionary, random, knee-rule, etc.).
